2. C-01 — CLOSE DIRECT CLIENT WALLET BALANCE INFLATION

Confirmed audit problem

The audit identified a dangerous branch in:

firestore.rules

Function:

isValidUserUpdate(userId)

The existing lastRewardId-related update branch permits authenticated users to modify additional wallet and reward-related fields without adequate restrictions.

Potentially affected fields include:

- balanceCoins
- balanceCents
- eligibleCoins
- promotionalCoins
- completedTasksCount
- checkInStreak
- extraSpinAvailable
- Other server-authoritative reward fields.

A user may manipulate their own Firestore document and potentially inflate withdrawable balances or poison leaderboard data.

Required remediation

A. Remove the insecure lastRewardId-based client wallet update authorization.

B. Ensure that normal users cannot directly modify any server-authoritative wallet or reward field.

C. Client profile updates must use a strict changedKeys().hasOnly(...) allowlist.

D. Keep only legitimate user-editable profile fields writable by the account owner.

E. Do not allow the user to modify:

- Wallet balances.
- Eligible balances.
- Promotional balances.
- Reward counters.
- Reward session state.
- Approval status.
- Role.
- Server-generated reward identifiers.
- Withdrawal accounting fields.
- Other financial or privileged fields.

F. Admin-authorized operations must also remain restricted to properly authenticated admins.

G. Inspect TaskFlowRepository.kt and remove direct client balance writes from handleLocalCallableFallback and any other insecure local reward fallback.

H. All financial credits, debits, bonuses, reversals and reward mutations must be performed by authorized server-side Cloud Functions using the Admin SDK and atomic Firestore transactions.

I. Do not break legitimate profile editing, profile initialization, or account approval workflows.

Required tests

Verify that:

- A user cannot set balanceCoins to an arbitrary value.
- A user cannot increase eligibleCoins.
- A user cannot increase promotionalCoins.
- A user cannot modify balanceCents.
- A user cannot change completedTasksCount.
- A user cannot manipulate checkInStreak.
- A user cannot increase extraSpinAvailable.
- A user cannot bypass restrictions by including lastRewardId.
- A user can still update permitted profile fields.
- Authorized server-side Cloud Functions can still credit rewards.
- Admin operations still work through their authorized server-side paths.

Test both allowed and denied operations using actual Firestore Rules tests where possible.

