4. C-03 — FIX PHASE 3E SERVER-ONLY CALLABLE GUARD AND REMOVE INSECURE FINANCIAL FALLBACKS

Confirmed audit problem

TaskFlowRepository.kt contains:

isServerOnlyCallable()
isCloudFunctionMissing(err)
handleLocalCallableFallback()

The audit found four Phase 3E callables missing from isServerOnlyCallable:

1. listUserEligibleTrackedCampaigns
2. listUserTrackedRewardActivity
3. adminListCampaignConversions
4. reviewCampaignConversion

The current fallback handling can incorrectly return:

mapOf("success" to true)

This can cause fake-success responses when a server operation actually failed.

The audit also found a dangerous promo fallback that can grant 500 TF for an arbitrary promo string if the Cloud Function fails.

Required remediation

A. Add all four Phase 3E callables to the correct server-only callable classification.

B. Review the complete callable registry. Identify every financial, reward, campaign, moderation, admin and security-sensitive callable.

C. Ensure that all such callables fail closed.

D. A timeout, unavailable function, permission error, internal server error or network error must never be converted into a successful financial operation.

E. Remove the 500 TF local promo redemption fallback completely.

F. Never credit promo rewards locally.

G. Never approve, reject or reverse a campaign conversion locally.

H. Never generate local success for a server-only operation.

I. Ensure that failed user campaign discovery requests display a genuine error state instead of silently pretending that the user has no eligible campaigns.

J. Ensure that failed user reward activity requests display an appropriate error state rather than silently returning an empty successful response.

K. Ensure that admin conversion moderation displays the actual server failure and refreshes the queue when appropriate.

L. Ensure that server-only callable errors preserve their original error codes and meaningful messages.

M. Avoid broad exception handling that converts unrelated errors into function-not-found errors.

N. Distinguish clearly between:

- NOT_FOUND / UNIMPLEMENTED function deployment problems.
- UNAVAILABLE / timeout / network errors.
- PERMISSION_DENIED.
- FAILED_PRECONDITION.
- INVALID_ARGUMENT.
- INTERNAL errors.

O. Do not use a local fallback for a financial operation just because Cloud Functions are temporarily unavailable.

P. Audit all existing handleLocalCallableFallback branches. Remove or disable insecure fallback behavior for:

- Promo redemption.
- Spin reward claims.
- Scratch Card reward claims.
- Daily Check-in reward claims.
- Manual Bonus.
- Campaign clicks.
- Campaign conversion moderation.
- Campaign reward activity.
- Wallet mutations.
- Any other server-authoritative financial operation.

Q. Preserve harmless non-financial fallback behavior only when it is demonstrably safe and does not simulate successful server execution.

R. Ensure that a server operation cannot be reported as successful unless the actual server response confirms success.

Required tests

Test all four Phase 3E callables with:

- Successful server response.
- NOT_FOUND.
- UNAVAILABLE.
- Timeout.
- PERMISSION_DENIED.
- INTERNAL.
- FAILED_PRECONDITION.

Verify no failure produces fake success.

Test arbitrary, invalid and expired promo codes under server failure.

Verify no local reward is credited.

Verify valid promo codes still work through the server.

Verify admin moderation only reports success after a successful server response.

Verify user tracking screens show genuine errors when the backend is unavailable.

